A||N||3||Eriamjh||Prothane Front Bushings: What is this?||||5||
Z||000000||Eriamjh||11-26-2001||09:00 PM||||OK, folks.  I'm no idiot, but I can't figure out what the "rings" are in my Prothane bushing kit for the front control arms!<P>Do they go on the other side of the lowers?<P>there are four of them and they look to be sized to go with the lower bushings.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tigger||11-26-2001||09:37 PM||||I think they do go on the other side, do they fit over the end of the bushing and metal sleeve?  I didn't realize this until after installing my bushings.  All I can say is I haven't had any problems without them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||11-26-2001||11:14 PM||||They should fit on the other side of the lowers. I think they are supposed to tighten up the front to back motion a little bit.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||11-27-2001||01:47 AM||||Those go on the "bare" side of the lowers, as DRH said.  You'll see that if you put the cupped side over the bushing on the inside section, they slip on just perfectly.  This is so you have poly on both sides of the bushing; it supports the arm a little better, and if things start to wear takes up the slack better.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
